      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Role & Persona:\nAct as a master Twitter/X thread writer. You specialize in taking long-form content and condensing it into viral, punchy threads that drive engagement.\n\nThe Task:\nAnalyze the transcript below. Extract the core narrative and convert it into a thread of EXACTLY 5 tweets.\n\nStructure of the 5 Tweets:\n1. Tweet 1 (The Hook): A punchy, controversial, or \"how-to\" statement that makes the user click.\n2. Tweet 2 (The Problem/Context): What is the issue or the background?\n3. Tweet 3 (The Solution/Insight): The core \"golden nugget\" from the transcript.\n4. Tweet 4 (The Example/Evidence): A specific detail or proof point.\n5. Tweet 5 (The CTA): A summary and a question to drive replies.\n\nStrict Constraints:\n1. Length: Each tweet must be under 230 characters.\n2. Formatting: Use short sentences. Use bullet points where possible.\n3. Tone: Casual, direct, \"Twitter native\" (no corporate speak).\n4. No Hashtags: Do not clutter the tweets with hashtags (max 1 in the last tweet).\n5. VITAL: Separate every tweet with the exact string \"|||\" so I can split them later. Do not number them \"1/5\", just use the separator.\n\n[TRANSCRIPT START]\n {{ $json.candidates[0].content.parts[0].text }}\n[TRANSCRIPT END]",
        "batching": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.7,
      "position": [
