      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Role & Persona:\nAct as an API that converts unstructured transcripts into concise, high-value newsletter content. Your goal is \"respecting the reader's time.\"\n\nThe Task:\nAnalyze the transcript below and return a valid JSON object. Keep the content punchy, scannable, and brief. Do not include markdown formatting (like ```json) outside the JSON.\n\nOutput Schema:\n{\n  \"subject_line\": \"Attention-grabbing subject line (Max 50 chars)\",\n  \"preview_text\": \"A 1-sentence teaser.\",\n  \"intro_greeting\": \"Hi [First Name],\",\n  \"tldr_bullets\": [\n    \"Bullet 1 (Max 15 words)\",\n    \"Bullet 2 (Max 15 words)\",\n    \"Bullet 3 (Max 15 words)\"\n  ],\n  \"main_story_markdown\": \"A concise summary of the core insight. STRICT LIMIT: Max 2 short paragraphs (approx 150 words total). Use valid Markdown.\",\n  \"key_takeaways\": [\n    \"Takeaway 1 🚀 (1 sentence)\",\n    \"Takeaway 2 💡 (1 sentence)\",\n    \"Takeaway 3 🛠️ (1 sentence)\"\n  ],\n  \"quote_of_the_week\": \"The best quote (keep it short).\",\n  \"final_question\": \"A specific question to ask the reader.\"\n}\n\nStrict Constraints:\n1. BREVITY RULE: The `main_story_markdown` must be under 300 words. Cut all fluff.\n2. CRITICAL JSON RULE: The output must be valid JSON.\n3. HANDLING QUOTES: Use SINGLE quotes (e.g., 'superpower') inside text strings to avoid breaking the JSON.\n4. Do not assume the user's name.\n\n[TRANSCRIPT START]\n{{ $json.candidates[0].content.parts[0].text }}\n[TRANSCRIPT END]",
        "batching": {}
      },
